Z||000000||Loki||08-08-2001||10:31 PM||||OK heres the deal. 86 SE V6 Auto.  Around town it drives great... After long distances though (say 30+ miles)   After cruising speeds if I have to slow down say under 3500 rpms, and then get back into the gas the car acts up. Stumbles real back, backfires and no power...I pull over let it sit for say 10 minutes and it goes just fine. Im thinking somehting is getting to hot. Dist, cap/rotor,module or coil?????  Or something else entirely...????? PLease help<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000001||Loki||08-09-2001||07:01 AM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||08-09-2001||10:13 AM||||Sounds like the ignition module to me. They get heat sensitive. also the coil could cause these symptoms.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000003||starfighter007@msn.com||08-09-2001||11:28 AM||||I would say that it is ingnition related, But I would also check fuel pump to be on the safe side.Have you tryed to let it sit and idle to see if you have a problem like you describe when you drive it? And I also wonder if the converter could be the problem? Like maybe getting clogged under load.<p>[This message has been edited by starfighter007@msn.com (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||RKM||08-09-2001||01:12 PM||||I agree that ignition seems likely.  I had the same problem on an 86 GT and it was the pickup coil in the distributor failing when hot.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Loki||08-09-2001||04:41 PM||||Well its not the cat. As its hollowed out (previous owner)  Coil has been replaced.  As long as im not on the gas it runs fine, at idle its a bit over 1000 rpm's  but runs smooth until i get on the gas.  Let it set with everyhting off for about 10 minutes it works fine till it heats back up.<BR> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mickey_Moose||08-09-2001||10:32 PM||||I also had the same problem and it was the pickup coil in the distributor - was also VERY intermittant for me as well.<P>Tim||||reg||1
